    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="0956" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg852"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/612a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-03-11T19:00:00-05:00">March 11, 1932—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Please confer immediately with the Commander of the Guardia and report in
                    detail by first possible air mail the plans for carrying out the policy as set
                    forth in the memorandum of February 5, 1931,<anchor n="49" xml:id="d868-f1"/> in
                    so far as it relates to turning over the Guardia Nacional to Nicaraguan
                    control.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
